Q: how to navigate from one page to another in react js? A: <p>==&gt; npm install react-router-dom</p>
<p>==&gt;Define your application routes in your main file (e.g., <code>App.jsx</code>). You create a router configuration and pass it to a <code>RouterProvide</code></p>
<pre><code>import { createBrowserRouter, RouterProvider } from 'react-router-dom';
import Home from './pages/Home';
import About from './pages/About';
import Profile from './pages/Profile';

const router = createBrowserRouter([
  {
    path: &quot;/&quot;,
    element: &lt;Home /&gt;,
  },
  {
    path: &quot;/about&quot;,
    element: &lt;About /&gt;,
  },
  {
    path: &quot;/profile/:username&quot;, // Dynamic route
    element: &lt;Profile /&gt;,
  },
]);

function App() {
  return &lt;RouterProvider router={router} /&gt;;
}

export default App;
</code></pre>
<p><code>==&gt;To navigate between pages using clickable elements, use the </code></p>
<pre><code>import { Link } from 'react-router-dom';

function Navbar() {
  return (
    &lt;nav&gt;
      &lt;Link to=&quot;/&quot;&gt;Home&lt;/Link&gt;
      &lt;Link to=&quot;/about&quot;&gt;About&lt;/Link&gt;
    &lt;/nav&gt;
  );
}
</code></pre>
<p>To trigger navigation automatically after an action (like submitting a form or clicking a button), use the <code>useNavigate</code> hook.</p>
<pre><code>import { useNavigate } from 'react-router-dom';

function LoginForm() {
  const navigate = useNavigate();

  const handleLogin = () =&gt; {
    // 1. Authenticate user logic here
    // 2. Redirect to dashboard programmatically
    navigate('/dashboard');
  };

  return &lt;button onClick={handleLogin}&gt;Log In&lt;/button&gt;;
}
</code></pre>

Q: Why am I getting a function error when using replace() to replace strings in a table? A: <p>As error hints, try explicit casts:</p>
<pre><code>UPDATE raw_data_file SET status = replace (status, 'PASS1_SUCCEEDED'::text, 'S3UPLOAD_SUCCEEDED'::text);
</code></pre>
<p>Btw, if your <code>status</code> field always contains only ONE of these text (so it cant contains things like <code>PASS1_SUCCEEDED;PASS2_SUCCEEDED</code>, you dont need string replace, you can simply do</p>
<pre><code>UPDATE raw_data_file SET status = 'S3UPLOAD_SUCCEEDED' WHERE status = 'PASS1_SUCCEEDED';
</code></pre>
